Planer EveryDay - full web planner (desktop folder untouched)

What is inside
- dashboard with stats, search, quick add and AI assistant
- calendar with CRUD tasks
- today page with focus advice and status toggles
- account page and settings page
- email/password auth
- JWT for API + web session for browser use
- OAuth routes for Yandex and VK (need provider credentials)

Quick start
1. Create venv
   py -m venv .venv
2. Activate
   .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
3. Install deps
   python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
4. Configure DB and secrets (copy .env.example manually into your environment if needed)
5. Run
   python app\core\main.py

Default DB values in app/core/DB.py
- dbname: planer_db
- user: postgres
- password: postgres123
- host: localhost
- port: 5432

OAuth notes
- Yandex login uses OAuth authorization and token exchange on the backend.
- VK login is scaffolded the same way, but both providers require real client_id/client_secret and redirect URI setup.
- If credentials are empty, provider buttons redirect back with an error.

API auth
- login/register return access_token and refresh_token
- API accepts Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
- browser pages also work with server session after login
